      "parameters": {
        "resource": "image",
        "operation": "analyze",
        "modelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "models/gemini-2.5-pro",
          "mode": "list",
          "cachedResultName": "models/gemini-2.5-pro"
        },
        "text": "You are a glass quotation assistant for OWD Glass. This is an architectural drawing showing a complete glass installation. Analyze this image THOROUGHLY and extract EVERY glass item visible.\n\nCRITICAL: This is a COMPLEX installation with multiple units. Look for:\n- All windows (different sizes, sliding, fixed, casement)\n- All doors (sliding doors, balcony doors, entry doors)\n- All glass panels (fixed, corner units, side panels)\n- Any glass partitions or walls\n\nFor EACH glass item you can identify, extract:\n- width_mm: Width in millimeters (convert from inches if needed: 1 inch = 25.4mm)\n- height_mm: Height in millimeters (convert from inches if needed: 1 inch = 25.4mm)\n- type: \"window\", \"door\", \"sliding_door\", \"fixed_panel\", or \"partition\"\n- glassType: Use industry-standard terms:\n  * \"clear\" for standard clear glass\n  * \"low-e\" for energy efficient/low emissivity glass\n  * \"tinted\" for colored/tinted glass\n  * \"frosted\" for obscure/frosted glass\n  * \"mirror\" for mirror glass\n  * \"patterned\" for decorative/patterned glass\n  * \"tempered\" for tempered safety glass\n  * \"laminated\" for laminated safety glass\n- frameColor: \"White\", \"Charcoal\", \"Brown\", \"Black\", \"Aluminum\", \"Silver\", or other visible frame color\n- thickness: glass thickness in mm (standard: 6mm for windows, 10-12mm for doors/sliding)\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- Count ALL glass units visible in the drawing\n- Look for dimension labels and measurements on the drawing\n- If measurements are shown in feet/inches, convert to mm (1 inch = 25.4mm)\n- Estimate sizes for unlabeled units based on scale and context\n- Include sliding glass doors, balcony doors, and large fixed panels\n- This appears to be a large installation - expect 8-15+ glass items\n- \"Low-E\" is commonly used for energy efficient glass in modern installations\n- Sliding doors and large panels typically use 10-12mm thickness\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON with ALL items:\n{\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"width_mm\": 1200,\n      \"height_mm\": 800,\n      \"type\": \"window\",\n      \"glassType\": \"clear\",\n      \"frameColor\": \"White\",\n      \"thickness\": 6\n    }\n  ]\n}",
        "options": {}
      },
